<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
    What Android may carry off this device, and what it may not.

    CLOUD BACKUP EXCLUDES EVERYTHING, AND THAT IS THE PRODUCT.

    GURU's promise is that the user's memory never leaves the phone. Shipping a person's
    brain, their conversations, their journal and their facts to Google Drive would break
    that promise in the exact place it is most valuable, and it would do so silently. So
    every domain is excluded from cloud backup, and that stays.

    DEVICE TRANSFER INCLUDES THE DATABASE AND FILES, AND THAT IS A DIFFERENT DECISION.

    Device transfer is a direct phone-to-phone migration the person initiates with a cable,
    with no account and no server involved. It cannot touch a cloud service, so it does not
    weaken the privacy promise by one inch. Excluding it meant that buying a new phone
    destroyed a year of a person's GURU with no recovery path and no warning, which is the
    failure this file previously caused.

    WHY THE WHOLE DATABASE DOMAIN RATHER THAN A NAMED FILE. guru_db lives in the database
    domain along with the rest, and a transfer rule that names one file inside a domain
    leaves every future database behind. The domain is the unit the platform offers, so it
    is the unit used here.

    SHARED PREFS TRAVEL BECAUSE THEY ARE PART OF THE BRAIN TOO. They hold the owner's model
    configuration, egress posture and heartbeat switch. Transferring the database without
    them would arrive on the new phone as a brain with no settings, which reads as a
    corrupted restore to the person holding it.

    CACHE AND EXTERNAL STORAGE STAY EXCLUDED. Cache is regenerable by definition, and
    external storage is shared with other apps, so neither belongs in a transfer of this
    app's own state.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external"  path="."/>
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="database" path="." />
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <include domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="cache" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
